    <h1>About ToolDrop</h1>
    
    <p>ToolDrop is a curated directory of AI tools specifically for <strong>vibe coders</strong> and <strong>indie game developers</strong>. We help you discover the best AI tools to accelerate your creative workflow.</p>
    
    <h2>🎯 What We Cover</h2>
    <p>We focus on AI tools across the entire game development and indie coding pipeline:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AI Coding Agents & IDEs</strong> - Code editors, autocomplete, and AI pair programmers</li>
      <li><strong>App Builders</strong> - Vibe coding tools that turn ideas into working apps</li>
      <li><strong>Code Review & Testing</strong> - Automated review, test generation, and QA</li>
      <li><strong>Game Art & Sprites</strong> - Image generation for game assets and concept art</li>
      <li><strong>3D & Models</strong> - AI-generated 3D models, textures, and environments</li>
      <li><strong>Audio, Music & SFX</strong> - AI music generation and sound effects</li>
      <li><strong>Voice</strong> - Text-to-speech, voice cloning, and dialogue generation</li>
      <li><strong>Game Design & Narrative</strong> - AI NPCs, storytelling, and quest design</li>
      <li><strong>Video & Trailers</strong> - AI video generation and editing</li>
      <li><strong>Marketing & Store Page Copy</strong> - Copywriting and marketing content</li>
      <li><strong>Agent Frameworks</strong> - SDKs and frameworks for building AI agents</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>🔍 How We Select Tools</h2>
    <p>Every tool in our directory is:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Actively maintained and accessible</li>
      <li>Useful for game developers or vibe coders</li>
      <li>Verified with accurate pricing and links</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>📬 Stay Updated</h2>
    <p>We're building a weekly newsletter to keep you updated on new AI tool releases, updates, and tips. The newsletter is coming soon!</p>
    
    <h2>🤝 Suggest a Tool</h2>
    <p>Know an AI tool that should be listed? We're always looking to expand our directory. Check out our <a href="https://github.com/tooldrop/tooldrop.github.io">GitHub repository</a> to contribute or suggest tools.</p>
    
    <h2>📖 Open Source</h2>
    <p>ToolDrop is open source. You can view the source code, contribute, or suggest improvements on <a href="https://github.com/tooldrop/tooldrop.github.io">GitHub</a>.</p>
